SUMMARY:LFS Feminist Consciousness-Raising Film Afternoons
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Freethought Society\n**Feminist Film Afternoons #1: 
 Made in Dagenham (2010)**\n\n**What happens when women stop cooperating wi
 th a system that depends on their labor but refuses to value it?**\nJoin u
 s for the first of five Feminist Consciousness-Raising Film Afternoons\, f
 eaturing *Made in Dagenham*\, the spirited\, funny\, and inspiring true st
 ory of women workers at Ford's Dagenham factory in England.\nIn 1968\, wom
 en sewing machinists discover that their work has been classified as unski
 lled and paid less than men's. Rather than accept it\, they organize\, str
 ike\, and help launch a movement for equal pay.\n**After the film\, we'll 
 discuss:**\n\n* What changed when these women recognized their shared situ
 ation?\n* Why was withdrawing their labor more effective than simply deman
 ding fair treatment?\n* What could women accomplish today by collectively 
 withdrawing their cooperation from unequal systems?\n\nThis is a relaxed\,
  friendly afternoon of film and conversation—not a lecture or debate. Ev
 eryone is welcome to bring their own experiences and perspectives.\n**The 
 Details**\n\n* **When:** Sunday\, November 15\, 2–5 PM\n* **Where:** My 
 home in Millersville. Address provided privately to confirmed attendees.\n
 * **Seating:** Limited to six guests.\n* **Attendance:** Women have priori
 ty through Saturday. If spaces remain\, men may RSVP beginning Saturday\, 
 November 14 at noon. Please respect this reservation arrangement.\n* **Gue
 sts:** No additional guests\, please.\n\nThis is the first of five indepen
 dent film afternoons\, held every other Sunday through January 10. Come to
  one or come to several—there's no commitment to attend the entire serie
 s.\n**Bring your curiosity\, your ideas\, and your willingness to imagine 
 something better!**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-freethought-society/events/
 317146005/
