SUMMARY:LFS Feminist Consciousness-Raising Film Afternoons
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Freethought Society\n**Feminist Film Afternoons #2: 
 Salt of the Earth (1954)**\n\n**What happens when women discover that figh
 ting for their families isn't enough—they must fight for their own equal
 ity\, too?**\nJoin us for the second of five Feminist Consciousness-Raisin
 g Film Afternoons\, featuring *Salt of the Earth*\, a groundbreaking Ameri
 can film based on a real miners' strike in New Mexico.\nWhen Mexican-Ameri
 can miners strike against dangerous working conditions and discriminatory 
 wages\, a court injunction prevents the men from picketing. Their wives st
 ep forward to take their places\, while the men must assume responsibility
  for the households and children.\nWhat begins as support for their husban
 ds becomes something much more powerful: women discovering their own polit
 ical agency.\n**After the film\, we'll discuss:**\n\n* How did the women's
  understanding of their own oppression change through collective action?\n
 * What happened when men and women exchanged their traditional responsibil
 ities?\n* Can a movement for equality succeed if women remain subordinate 
 within that movement?\n\nThis is a relaxed\, friendly afternoon of film an
 d conversation—not a lecture or debate. Everyone is welcome to share the
 ir experiences and perspectives.\n**The Details**\n\n* **When:** Sunday\, 
 November 29\, 2–5 PM\n* **Where:** Private home in Millersville. Address
  provided individually to confirmed attendees.\n* **Seating:** Limited to 
 six guests.\n* **Attendance:** Women have priority through Saturday. If sp
 aces remain\, men may RSVP beginning Saturday\, November 28 at noon.\n* **
 Guests:** No additional guests\, please.\n\nEach film afternoon stands on 
 its own. Come to one or several—no preparation or ongoing commitment req
 uired.\n**Bring your curiosity\, your ideas\, and your willingness to imag
 ine something better!**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-freethought-society/events/
 317146053/
